# Wireless survey and software-defined radio: RECEIVE ONLY. The image is for
# incident response and threat hunting, so the radio slice answers one question
# ("is something transmitting here that is not in the asset inventory?") and
# never transmits itself. rtl-sdr (rtl_eeprom dongle check, rtl_power sweeps to
# CSV) and gqrx work with receive-only RTL2832U dongles; gqrx pulls the
# gr-osmosdr *library* it needs on its own. Dropped on purpose (snapshot-menu
# 0.2.4): gnuradio and gr-osmosdr (flowgraph tooling nobody builds during an
# incident, ~350 MiB with SciPy/PyQt), soapysdr-tools (only useful with
# per-device modules and GNU Radio) and hackrf (transmit-capable hardware;
# red-team gear, not IR). The aircrack-ng package is here only for airodump-ng's
# passive 802.11 survey; Debian does not split it, so aireplay-ng and the
# cracker come along, but the menu exposes airodump-ng alone. (kismet is not in
# trixie: upstream apt repo only, not pinned here.)
aircrack-ng
rtl-sdr
gqrx-sdr
